<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- Build Settings -->
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>True</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>

    <!-- Package Info -->
    <Version>3.1.0</Version>
    <Title>Portamical</Title>
    <Authors>CsabaDu</Authors>
    <Company>CsabaDu</Company>
    <Description>Shared utilities and base classes for cross‑framework test data solutions in .NET, built on the Portamical.Core data model.</Description>
    <Copyright>(c) 2026. Csaba Dudas (CsabaDu)</Copyright>

    <!-- Package Assets -->
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE.txt</PackageLicenseFile>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>True</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>

    <!-- Repository -->
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/CsabaDu/Portamical/tree/master/Portamical</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageTags>test; unittest; testdata; frameworkagnostic; portable; dynamicdata; datadriven; async; mstest; nunit; xunit; xunitv3; tunit;</PackageTags>

    <!-- Release Notes -->
    <PackageReleaseNotes>v3.1.0 - 2026-05-27

Added
- **MetadataEquality&lt;TException&gt;(TException, TException, Action&lt;string, string?&gt;)** - New public synchronous wrapper for exception metadata assertions
  - Enables framework-agnostic verification of exception messages and parameter names
  - Delegates to MetadataEqualityAsync via thread-safe synchronous execution
  - Supports ArgumentException, ArgumentOutOfRangeException, ObjectDisposedException with intelligent message filtering

Changed
- **MetadataEqualityAsync&lt;TException&gt;(TException, TException, Func&lt;string, string?, ValueTask&gt;)** - Made public (was private)
  - Primary async implementation for exception metadata verification
  - Intelligently handles framework-generated messages that vary across runtime versions
  - Skips assertion for ArgumentException guard clauses and ObjectDisposedException runtime-specific patterns
  - Includes comprehensive XML documentation with usage examples

Improved
- Enhanced XML documentation for both MetadataEqualityAsync and MetadataEquality methods
  - Detailed remarks explaining selective assertion logic for framework exceptions
  - Usage examples for TUnit (async) and NUnit (sync) scenarios
  - Performance notes and thread safety guidance</PackageReleaseNotes>
    
    <!-- Package Generation -->
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <PackageOutputPath>$(OutputPath)</PackageOutputPath>

    <!-- Symbols -->
    <IncludeSymbols>True</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\icon.png">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\LICENSE.txt">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Portamical.Core" Version="2.2.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Update="README.md">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
